# Workflows under .github/ get privileged execution: sign.yml runs on the
# self-hosted runner that holds the "Obsidian Systems" signing key, on every
# merge to main. A change here is therefore a change to what runs next to that
# key, so it needs a named reviewer rather than a casual approval.
#
# This gates merging only. It has no bearing on fork pull requests, which never
# merge -- those are governed by the fork-approval setting under
# Settings -> Actions -> General.
#
# Both maintainers are listed so either can review the other's CI changes;
# GitHub does not let an author approve their own pull request.
/.github/        @manuel-os-work @patrickaldis
